[h1]Questions[/h1]
Ask anything about Inventory Enhancer here: how sorting or filtering works, whether something is possible, compatibility with another mod, install trouble that is not a bug. One question per reply keeps answers easy to find. Bugs go in the Bug Reports thread, ideas in the Suggestions thread.

[h2]Already answered[/h2]
[list]
    [*][b]How many sort categories are there?[/b] 13: Name, Tier, Damage, Accuracy, Reach, Missile Speed, Hit Points, Armor Total, Armor Highest, Speed, Handling, Weight, and Value / Weight, grouped under General, Combat, and Defense.
    [*][b]How many filter categories are there?[/b] 34: 30 category filters across seven groups (Melee One-Handed, Melee Two-Handed, Shields & Ranged, Armor, Mounts, Misc, Culture), plus 4 modifier filters (High Tier, Low Tier, High Value, Low Value).
    [*][b]How do category filters and modifier filters combine?[/b] Category filters use OR logic (an item shows if it matches any selected category); the modifiers then use AND logic to narrow whatever the categories already matched.
    [*][b]Does search work in the loot screen?[/b] Yes. The search bar is enabled in inventories where the game normally disables it, including loot screens, and matching is case-insensitive.
    [*][b]Can I keep my sort and filter choices between inventory openings?[/b] Yes, turn on "Remember Selections" in MCM; it is off by default.
    [*][b]What does the culture filter go by?[/b] The item's actual culture (Vlandian, Sturgian, Imperial, Battanian, Khuzait, Aserai), not its name or source mod.
[/list]

[h2]When asking[/h2]
Say which Bannerlord version you run and which screen (inventory, loot, trade) the question concerns.
